  "scope": "PL4-owned ISidedInventory fallback and explicit LegacySidedInventory instances only. Existing provider-advertised IItemHandler capabilities keep their original path.",
  "contract": {
    "mapping": "Capture a bounded prefix of native getSlotsForFace indices once per adapter, excluding invalid and duplicate physical indices while retaining first occurrence and raw positions.",
    "bounds": "At most min(raw length, configured slot limit,4096) raw indices scanned during construction; invalid and duplicate entries consume the prefix budget. Each subsequent slot check compares its captured raw position and physical index, without a full array rescan or allocation by PL4.",
    "permissions": "Recheck native canExtractItem/canInsertItem for the captured face before delegating physical-slot transfers to Forge InvWrapper, retaining native simulation, item validity, stack limits and dirty marking.",
    "stale_mapping": "Known physical identity participates in row comparison and pre-extraction fencing. Captured adapters refuse changed or in-place edited slot positions rather than silently redirecting operations.",
    "aliases": "PL4-owned adapters expose their backing object/physical slot for deduplication across overlapping faces and same-network uncertainty fencing.",
    "provider_ownership": "A target advertising an item capability still returns that original handler. General provider SidedInvWrapper/CombinedInvWrapper backings remain opaque.",
    "natural_faces": "When every item route for a target is a PL4-owned sided adapter, retain the separate face routes and deduplicate their physical slots, so disjoint slots survive. Mixed or opaque target routes keep the prior conservative target-level policy."
  },
